  - [1m[38;5;153mComment[0m — [38;5;153mtask[39m FK, [38;5;153mauthor[39m FK, body, [38;5;153mcreated_at[39m. Needed in spec 1 because commenting is one of the three involvement
    triggers.
  - [1m[38;5;153mEvent[0m — [38;5;153mtask[39m FK, [38;5;153mactor[39m FK, [38;5;153mverb[39m, [38;5;153mpayload[39m (JSON: before/after), [38;5;153mcreated_at[39m. Verbs: [38;5;153mcreated[39m, [38;5;153mtitle_changed[39m,
    [38;5;153mdescription_changed[39m, [38;5;153mstatus_changed[39m, [38;5;153massigned[39m, [38;5;153munassigned[39m, [38;5;153mdue_date_changed[39m, [38;5;153mcommented[39m. Append-only, never updated
    or deleted.

  [1mModels in spec 2:[0m

  - [1m[38;5;153mSubscription[0m — [38;5;153muser[39m + [38;5;153mtask[39m (unique together), [38;5;153mstate[39m ∈ [38;5;153mwatching[39m | [38;5;153mmuted[39m, [38;5;153mreason[39m ∈ [38;5;153mcreator[39m | [38;5;153massignee[39m | [38;5;153mcommenter[39m |
    [38;5;153mmanual[39m. Muting writes a real row rather than deleting one, so that later involvement doesn't silently re-subscribe
    someone who opted out. That's the detail most implementations get wrong.
  - [1m[38;5;153mNotification[0m — [38;5;153muser[39m FK, [38;5;153mevent[39m FK (unique together), [38;5;153mread_at[39m nullable, [38;5;153memailed_at[39m nullable, [38;5;153mcreated_at[39m.
  - [1m[38;5;153mNotificationPreference[0m — [38;5;153muser[39m one-to-one, [38;5;153memail_mode[39m ∈ [38;5;153mbatched[39m | [38;5;153mdigest[39m | [38;5;153moff[39m. One row per user, created on signup.

  [1mTwo rules baked into the model rather than the UI:[0m the fan-out never creates a [38;5;153mNotification[39m where [38;5;153mevent.actor == user[39m
  (no self-notification), and [38;5;153mNotification[39m is unique on (user, event) so a retried worker can't double-send.

  [1mOne open question I'm not going to answer for you.[0m There's no grouping concept here — no lists, projects, or tags. For
  5–50 people sharing one flat task pile, that may get unpleasant fast. I left it out because you didn't ask for it and
  the care-model we chose is per-task rather than per-list, so notifications don't need it. But it's cheaper to add now
  than later.
